==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|five by five}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-five-by-five.wav|a=US}}

===Etymology 1===
From radio communications phrase dating from the 1950s. The first five referred to a rating of signal clarity, the other to reception strength. See {{pedia|Signal strength and readability report}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{cap|loud and clear}}.
#* {{quote-web|en|author=w:Howard Tayler|work=w:Schlock Mercenary|date=13 December 2019|url=https://www.schlockmercenary.com/2019-12-13|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250213030347/https://www.schlockmercenary.com/2019-12-13|archivedate=13 February 2025|accessdate=12 February 2025|text="Hon, are you getting good data from us?"  "'''Five-by-five'''."  "Any sign of hostiles?"  "Nope."  "Can I get a few more syllables from you?"}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Harry Blank|chapter=Not Ready for Prime Time|chapterurl=https://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/54-not-ready-for-prime-time|title=Deadlined|date=28 September 2024|page=602|isbn=9798338449400|text=McInnis nodded, and Carter keyed the mic. "CAONCI-Site-43 calling Overwatch Command," he intoned in his best radio voice. Veiksaar smirked. "CAONCI-Site-43, Overwatch Command. Do you read?"<br>The response came immediately, to the visible relief of all nine of them. Even Wettle. "'''Five by five''', CAONCI-Site-43. '''Five by five'''."}}
# {{cap|fine}}; [[OK]].

