===Etymology 2===

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|basketball}} A [[performance]] in which a [[player]] [[accumulate]]s [[five]] [[point]]s in each of five [[statistical]] [[category|categories]] ([[point]]s, [[rebound]]s, [[assist]]s, [[steal]]s{{,}} and [[block]]s) in a [[single]] [[game]].
# {{lb|en|slang}} Someone whose [[body]] is [[roughly]] [[shape]]d like a [[square#Noun|square]]; a [[short#Adjective|short]] and [[fat#Adjective|fat]] person.
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:fat person}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Warren Eyster|title=Ear From the Customary Skies|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:Random House|year=1953|page=335|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/earfromcustomary0000unse/page/335/mode/1up|passage="Yeah? No stuff? You, a date? Wad yuh know. What is she, a '''five-by-five'''?"}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Jeremiah Healy|title=The Only Good Lawyer: A John Francis Cuddy Mystery|location=New York, N.Y.{{nb...}}|publisher=w:Pocket Books|year=1998|page=71|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/onlygoodlawyerjo00heal/page/71/mode/1up|isbn=0-671-00953-2|passage="The muscle was Oscar Huong, a real Mr. '''five-by-five'''. Father supposedly a black Marine boxing champion. The brains was Nguyen Trinh—or 'Nugey,' for short. He had no idea who his daddy was."}}

